<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/cnce/cnce.jpg", "Homemade CNC engraver" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Improvised Motion</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        The engraver was built from salvaged optical-drive mechanics, which made it a compact way to
        learn how stepper motion, guides, backlash and frame stiffness interact.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        It was not about creating a production machine. It was about making a limited set of parts
        move predictably enough to engrave and learning from every compromise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--reverse">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      <video class="media__el" controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/assets/images/projects/cnce/cover.png">
        <source src="/assets/images/projects/cnce/demo.mp4" type="video/quicktime">
      </video>
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Control</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        The controller side introduced me to GRBL-style motion control, wiring discipline and the
        practical difference between a movement that works once and a setup that behaves repeatably.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        As an early project, it became a useful foundation for later CNC and machining work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

